# Real appsettings files may hold live secrets (DB password, JWT signing key, Gemini API key) - only
# the placeholder appsettings.Example.json is ever tracked. Ignoring the bare name (not just
# *.local.json/*.Development.json) means a real file can never be committed by accident even via
# `git add -A`, regardless of what environment suffix it uses.
appsettings.json
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.Example.json
# Data Protection keys encrypt PATs at rest - never commit them (losing/leaking them is either a
# security incident or makes every stored PAT permanently unreadable).
DataProtection-Keys/
